      <h2 id="flexvolume-drivers_persistent-storage-flexvolume" class="group scroll-mt-20">About FlexVolume drivers<a href="#flexvolume-drivers_persistent-storage-flexvolume" class="ml-2 text-muted-foreground opacity-0 group-hover:opacity-100 no-underline" aria-hidden="true" tabindex="-1">&para;</a></h2>
      <p class="_abstract">When working with FlexVolume drivers, it is helpful to understand how OpenShift Container Platform interact with the drivers.</p>
      <p>A FlexVolume driver is an executable file that resides in a well-defined directory on all nodes in the cluster. OpenShift Container Platform calls the FlexVolume driver whenever it needs to mount or unmount a volume represented by a <code>PersistentVolume</code> object with <code>flexVolume</code> as the source.</p>
      <Alert variant="info" class="my-4">
