      <h2 id="flexvolume-driver-example_persistent-storage-flexvolume" class="group scroll-mt-20">FlexVolume driver example<a href="#flexvolume-driver-example_persistent-storage-flexvolume" class="ml-2 text-muted-foreground opacity-0 group-hover:opacity-100 no-underline" aria-hidden="true" tabindex="-1">&para;</a></h2>
      <p class="_abstract">When working with FlexVolume drivers, it is helpful to become familiar with structure of the driver.</p>
      <p>The first command-line argument of the FlexVolume driver is always an operation name. Other parameters are specific to each operation. Most of the operations take a JavaScript Object Notation (JSON) string as a parameter. This parameter is a complete JSON string, and not the name of a file with the JSON data.</p>
      <p>The FlexVolume driver contains:</p>
      <ul>
      <li>All <code>flexVolume.options</code>.</li>
      <li>Some options from <code>flexVolume</code> prefixed by <code>kubernetes.io/</code>, such as <code>fsType</code> and <code>readwrite</code>.</li>
      <li>The content of the referenced secret, if specified, prefixed by <code>kubernetes.io/secret/</code>.</li>
      </ul>
      <CodeBlock code={"{\n\t\"fooServer\": \"192.168.0.1:1234\",\n        \"fooVolumeName\": \"bar\",\n\t\"kubernetes.io/fsType\": \"ext4\",\n\t\"kubernetes.io/readwrite\": \"ro\",\n\t\"kubernetes.io/secret/<key name>\": \"<key value>\",\n\t\"kubernetes.io/secret/<another key name>\": \"<another key value>\",\n}"} lang="json" title="FlexVolume driver JSON input example" />
      <p>where:</p>
      <dl class="my-4 space-y-2">
      <dt class="font-semibold"><code>fooServer</code></dt>
      <dd class="ml-6 text-muted-foreground"><p>Specifies all options from <code>flexVolume.options</code>.</p></dd>
      <dt class="font-semibold"><code>kubernetes.io/fsType</code></dt>
      <dd class="ml-6 text-muted-foreground"><p>Specifies the value of <code>flexVolume.fsType</code>.</p></dd>
      <dt class="font-semibold"><code>kubernetes.io/readwrite</code></dt>
      <dd class="ml-6 text-muted-foreground"><p>Specifies the value <code>ro</code> or <code>rw</code> based on <code>flexVolume.readOnly</code>.</p></dd>
      <dt class="font-semibold"><code>kubernetes.io/secret/&lt;key name&gt;</code></dt>
      <dd class="ml-6 text-muted-foreground"><p>Specifies all keys and their values from the secret referenced by <code>flexVolume.secretRef</code>.</p></dd>
      </dl>
      <p>OpenShift Container Platform expects JSON data on standard output of the driver. When not specified, the output describes the result of the operation.</p>
      <CodeBlock code={"{\n\t\"status\": \"<Success/Failure/Not supported>\",\n\t\"message\": \"<Reason for success/failure>\"\n}"} lang="json" title="FlexVolume driver default output example" />
      <p>Exit code of the driver should be <code>0</code> for success and <code>1</code> for error.</p>
      <p>Operations should be idempotent, which means that the mounting of an already mounted volume should result in a successful operation.</p>
